---
description: Keep type declarations isolated from runtime logic
alwaysApply: true
---

# Typing Separation Standard

- Prefer moving non-trivial type declarations out of service/page files.
- Use dedicated files for types:
  - domain types -> `*.types.ts`
  - request/response contracts -> `dto/*` or `contracts/*`
  - shared cross-app types -> `packages/shared`
- Keep inline types only when they are short, local, and used once.
- Avoid large type blocks mixed with business logic in the same file.
- Export named types (avoid default exports for types).

## Naming
- Runtime constants/functions and types must be clearly separable by filename and import path.
- If a file grows many `type`/`interface` declarations, split by domain context.
